prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "gh pr create --draft --repo vercel/api --base main --head mk/elastic-build-machines-v9 --title \"[@api/build-machines] add elastic v9 shadow\" --body $'## Why/Summary\\n\\n- Reintroduce the sustained-CPU upgrade candidate after V8 promotion, now as V9, so production logs compare current V8 decisions against the CPU-driven upgrade rule.\\n- Keep V8 as the effective algorithm and preserve its low-CPU duration-upgrade guard inside V9; V9 only adds sustained CPU-driven upgrades on top.\\n- Log V9 shadow decisions and CPU pressure buckets via the existing decision log so Datadog can monitor `v8*` vs `v9*` decisions.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- Covered V9 sustained-CPU upgrades, peak-only CPU spikes, sample-count guardrails, V8 low-CPU upgrade guard carryover, V8/V6 CPU downgrade guard behavior, memory upgrades, build-span scoping, and OOM behavior.\\n'"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["git", "-C", "/Users/mehulkar/dev/vercel/vercel-core/api", "branch", "-d", "mehulkar/move-service-checks"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "gh pr create --draft --repo vercel/api --base main --head mk/promote-elastic-v9 --title \"[@api/build-machines] promote elastic v9, drop v8\" --body $'## Why/Summary\\n\\n- Promote V9 so elastic build machines can upgrade on sustained CPU pressure, keeping the current heuristic: CPU >90% for >50% of build-window samples with at least 3 samples.\\n- We are choosing this heuristic because it looks like a good balance: it catches a small CPU-bound tail with minimal overall impact, while lower thresholds were materially broader and higher thresholds nearly disabled the signal.\\n- Shadow data shows the affected right-sizing is overwhelmingly `standard` -> `enhanced`, which is the expected shape for the first CPU-pressure upgrade trigger.\\n\\n## Shadow Results\\n\\n[Datadog v8 vs v9 decision breakdown](https://app.datadoghq.com/logs?query=service%3Asubscriber-elastic-build-machines%20%22elastic%20decision%22%20%40decision.current%3Av8%2A%20%40decision.next%3Av9%2A&agg_m=count&agg_m_source=base&agg_q=%40decision.nextVsCurrent%2C%40decision.current&agg_t=count&analyticsOptions=%5B%22bars%22%2C%22dog_classic%22%2Cnull%2Cnull%2C%22value%22%5D&clustering_pattern_field_path=message&cols=%40hw.memory.summary.peak%2C%40hw.cpu.summary.peak%2C%40decision.current%2C%40decision.next%2C%40deployment&flat_group_bys=true&fromUser=true&messageDisplay=inline&refresh_mode=sliding&sort_m=count&sort_t=count&storage=hot&stream_sort=time%2Cdesc&top_n=100&top_o=top&viz=sunburst&x_missing=true&from_ts=1780501937575&to_ts=1780588337575&live=true)\\n\\nValidation window: 2026-06-04 17:12 UTC to 2026-06-05 17:12 UTC.\\n\\n| Result | Count |\\n| --- | ---: |\\n| Total v8 -> v9 decisions | ~285k |\\n| `same` | ~99% |\\n| `above` | ~2.5k (~0.88%) |\\n| `below` | 0 |\\n\\n`above` split in the validation window:\\n\\n| Transition | Count |\\n| --- | ---: |\\n| `v8-no-change-standard` -> `v9-upgrade-enhanced` | 2,425 |\\n| `v8-no-change-enhanced` -> `v9-upgrade-turbo` | 46 |\\n\\nThreshold analysis for net-new READY-build upgrades relative to V8:\\n\\n| Sample threshold | CPU >70% | CPU >80% | CPU >90% | CPU >95% |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\n| `>= 25%` | `76,115` (`26.66%`) | `55,696` (`19.51%`) | `31,386` (`10.99%`) | `16,822` (`5.78%`) |\\n| `>= 40%` | `23,397` (`8.19%`) | `12,266` (`4.30%`) | `6,081` (`2.13%`) | `3,390` (`1.16%`) |\\n| `>= 50%` | `9,280` (`3.25%`) | `5,720` (`2.00%`) | `2,504` (`0.88%`) | `884` (`0.30%`) |\\n| `>= 60%` | `4,176` (`1.46%`) | `2,070` (`0.72%`) | `470` (`0.16%`) | `107` (`0.04%`) |\\n| `>= 75%` | `587` (`0.21%`) | `301` (`0.11%`) | `11` (`<0.01%`) | `1` (`<0.01%`) |\\n| `>= 90%` | `5` (`<0.01%`) | `0` (`0%`) | `0` (`0%`) | `0` (`0%`) |\\n\\n## What\\n\\n- Set V9 as the current elastic algorithm and disable shadow mode.\\n- Drop V8 now that V9 carries forward V8 behavior and adds the sustained CPU-pressure upgrade trigger.\\n'"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "{ datadog-query search-logs --query \"service:subscriber-elastic-build-machines \\\"elastic decision\\\" @decision.current:v8* @decision.next:v9* @decision.nextVsCurrent:above\" --from \"2026-06-04T17:12:17Z\" --to \"2026-06-04T23:12:17Z\" --limit 1000 | jq -r '.data.data[].attributes.attributes.projectId'; datadog-query search-logs --query \"service:subscriber-elastic-build-machines \\\"elastic decision\\\" @decision.current:v8* @decision.next:v9* @decision.nextVsCurrent:above\" --from \"2026-06-04T23:12:17Z\" --to \"2026-06-05T05:12:17Z\" --limit 1000 | jq -r '.data.data[].attributes.attributes.projectId'; datadog-query search-logs --query \"service:subscriber-elastic-build-machines \\\"elastic decision\\\" @decision.current:v8* @decision.next:v9* @decision.nextVsCurrent:above\" --from \"2026-06-05T05:12:17Z\" --to \"2026-06-05T11:12:17Z\" --limit 1000 | jq -r '.data.data[].attributes.attributes.projectId'; datadog-query search-logs --query \"service:subscriber-elastic-build-machines \\\"elastic decision\\\" @decision.current:v8* @decision.next:v9* @decision.nextVsCurrent:above\" --from \"2026-06-05T11:12:17Z\" --to \"2026-06-05T17:12:17Z\" --limit 1000 | jq -r '.data.data[].attributes.attributes.projectId'; } | sort -u | wc -l"], decision="allow")
